[[Image:Isk x2cweap.gif|right|Craft weapon]]
The character knows how to create most types of weapons and ammunition from different materials.
*'''Ability:''' [[intelligence]]

*'''Classes:''' [[arcane archer]], [[assassin]], [[barbarian]], [[bard]], [[blackguard]], [[champion of Torm]], [[cleric]], [[druid]], [[dwarven defender]], [[fighter]], [[Harper scout]], [[monk]], [[paladin]], [[pale master]], [[ranger]], [[red dragon disciple]], [[rogue]], [[shifter]], [[sorcerer]], [[wizard]]

*'''[[Cross-class skill]]:''' yes

*'''[[untrained skill check|Requires training]]:''' no

*'''Check:''' Based on the difficulty to craft this particular item (see in-game crafting menu)

*'''Use:''' Use crafting component

==Notes==
*Requires [[Hordes of the Underdark]].
*This skill cannot craft magical weapons by default, aside from two ironwood weapons (+1 attack and 40% weight).
*This skill can be used to modify the appearance of a weapon against a [[difficulty class]] of 15. The cost in gold to modify an item is (1/4 of the item's current value + 1) per part modified (this has a maximum value of the item cost + 1, but this is rarely reached as there are only three weapon parts); the full value is charged even when the skill check is unsuccessful.
:* [[Plot]] weapons, [[intelligent weapon]]s, [[sling]]s, and [[whip]]s cannot have their appearance modified.
* If a character has a modified score of 6 points in craft weapon or [[craft armor]], then creatures, placeables, and doors killed/destroyed by that character can drop basic crafting material based on their appearance (see creature articles for the material dropped). Of note is the "large bone" dropped by skeletal creatures, as it can be crafted into a bone wand which can then be used with the [[craft wand]] feat.
*This skill can be used to craft a weapon or weapon component from raw material. The gold cost, DC, and components are given below with a 1/4 gold cost charge and loss of components if the skill check is failed.
